	After seeing the recent flow of inquiries regarding MORIA, I feel
	that I should clear up a few things:

		o  To	my  knowledge,	and  the  author  Robert
		   Koeneke, there has not been a successful port
		   to any UNIX site (sorry folks).

		o  The current version of MORIA IS 4.8, 4.9 is a
		   minor bug fix version due out shortly.  MORIA
		   version  5.0  was  started on at one point in
		   time, but has yet to be completed.

	For  the past two years I have had the privilege of working with
	Robert  Koeneke  at  the  University  of  Oklahoma.  I have also
	become  a  hopeless  addict  of MORIA, but I think I'm over that
	now.

	Now  for the good news.  I WILL be distributing of MORIA for use
	by  other  confused  individuals  (be  warned  if you have never
	played  it).   Robert  will  NOT,  I repeat NOT, be distributing
	until further notice.  You may, however, direct fan mail his way
	(He is not sure what his network addresses are, so you will have
	to write).  He would love to hear about your amusements with the
	game,  but  do  not expect a reply.  He has recently taken a job
	with American Airlines in Tulsa, Oklahoma, and his address is:

			       Robert Koeneke
			       12706 E. 39th St.
			       Tulsa, OK  74146

	I  am  a  quite  busy individual, so all I can promise is that I
	will  get  it to all interested parties.  VMS Backup will be the
	distribution  format,  at either 1600 or 6250 bpi.  I am willing
	to  give out the source, and encourage people to propagate it on
	to  others.   Those  interested  should contact me (via personal
	mail preferably, NO phone calls before 5:00pm EST), or send me a
	tape with enough cash to mail it back to you.

	There,	I hope this answers everyones questions about the status
	of  MORIA.   Note  that  I  rarely read the games newsgroups, so
	please  send  your  inquiries  to me personally).  Long live the
	Balrog!!!

							-Bill Ouchark-

	P.S. - Anyone else out there interested in distributing?

